    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6fe76925_a6831e64",
        "filename": "common/temp_sensor.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146415
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-07-28T00:17:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added a ifdef since this function uses thermal_params to calculate the possible fan_percent based on the temperatures read from the sensors, fan_off and fan_max temperatures declared in thermal_params. With this change we define thermal params only when we want EC to control the thermal logic(thermal_control in thermal.c). Boards in which the thermal control is completely taken care by DPTF, thermal_params will not be available. Since CONFIG_THROTTLE_AP is the flag guarding both thermal.c and throttle_ap.c,  I think, CONFIG_THROTTLE_AP makes more sense. Ideally, I think printing fan percent here is not needed. As the function reads I think it should only print the temperatures read by sensors.",
      "parentUuid": "6fe76925_b2eb60e0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 25
      },
